    "created_at": "2022-03-08T21:28:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-08T21:28:59Z",
    "body": "Autofocus has used same-origin since before https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/4763 when it was rewritten, i.e. that rewrite just preserved it.\r\n\r\nThe check on the entire ancestor chain was introduced in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6204. There was some discussion at the time as to whether it was necessary, and I guess I pushed for it. The motivation was to avoid a cross-origin information leak, in nesting cases like A1 -> B -> A2. See https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6204#issuecomment-743313612 .\r\n\r\nI think that same motivation applies to dialog, and so it was an oversight that dialog was not updated.\r\n\r\nAs for same origin vs. same origin-domain, I think there would be no problem with loosening it to same origin-domain, since same origin-domain pages leak information and collaborate already. It's more just a question as to whether we want to be consistent (and thus use same origin-domain) or start moving away from that world as part of `document.domain` deprecation. Probably at this point we shouldn't change anything...",
